# A program that mentions a unit gets the standard families it names (Length, Time and what they need) injected from the units prelude. Those copies have their spans in the prelude text, not the program's, so the semantic index derives no record for them and stays complete: the struct and `run` still have one record apiece.
fixture: SemanticIndexSkipsInjectedUnitFamilies.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet inspect compiler check main.jet
exit: 0
json: stdout doc $.compiler.value.diagnostics #= 0
json: stdout doc $.compiler.value.semantic_index.derivations[?identity.target="core.compiler"] #= 2 # the struct and run, no injected family
json: stdout doc $.compiler.value.semantic_index.derivations[?claim="type:core_compiler.Trip"] #= 1
json: stdout doc $.compiler.value.semantic_index.derivations[?claim="fn:core_compiler.run"] #= 1
json: stdout doc $.compiler.value.semantic_index.derivations[?claim="type:core_compiler.Length"] #= 0 # an injected catalog family has no text here
